
===== PARTNER VERDICT (codex, 647s) =====

Implemented the optional BYO-key AI helper. No commit or deploy.

**Changed Files**
- [server/ai.js](Z:/328/CMPUT328-A2/codexworks/301/language/server/ai.js): new gated `POST /api/ai` handler.
- [server/app.js](Z:/328/CMPUT328-A2/codexworks/301/language/server/app.js): mounted `/api/ai` and `/language/api/ai`.
- [server/keyStore.js](Z:/328/CMPUT328-A2/codexworks/301/language/server/keyStore.js): server-only `getFirstSecret()` for the current user.
- [server/ai.test.ts](Z:/328/CMPUT328-A2/codexworks/301/language/server/ai.test.ts): no-key backend test.
- [src/App.tsx](Z:/328/CMPUT328-A2/codexworks/301/language/src/App.tsx): `AiStudyHelper` on learn, scene, kanji reference, and kanji recognition views.
- [vite.config.ts](Z:/328/CMPUT328-A2/codexworks/301/language/vite.config.ts): `/language/api` dev proxy.
- [vitest.config.ts](Z:/328/CMPUT328-A2/codexworks/301/language/vitest.config.ts): includes `server/**/*.test.ts`.

**Backend**
`POST /api/ai` is behind `requireSession`, loads only that user’s stored key, and calls OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions server-side. DeepSeek defaults to `https://api.deepseek.com` + `deepseek-chat`; other providers use stored `baseUrl` + `model`. Returns `{ reply }`; errors include `no_key` and safe `provider_error`. The key is never returned to the browser, and provider error messages redact key-shaped tokens.

**Frontend**
The helper is absent for signed-out users. Signed-in users without a key see a small Settings hint. Signed-in users with a key get an unobtrusive Ask AI panel with loading, reply, and error states. Requests use `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}api/ai` with credentials included.

